6 privacy policy", "OAIC ADM guidance", "Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024", "energy retailer hardship", "decision register", "OpenTelemetry legacy systems", "fractional CTO Australia", "AI governance Australia"], "faq": [["What changes on 10 December 2026?", "APP entities must include information in their privacy policy where they have arranged for a computer program to make, or do something substantially and directly related to making, decisions that significantly affect individuals, using personal information. The duty comes from the Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024."], ["Does human review take a decision out of scope?", "Not automatically. According to commentary on the OAIC's guidance, a decision can be in scope even when a program's output only informs a person who makes the final call, and the OAIC encourages treating borderline cases as in scope."], ["Is this only about AI?", "No. The OAIC's guidance reaches rules engines, scoring tools and other software that substantially informs significant decisions, not only machine learning."]], "related": ["/fractional-cto-australia/", "/ai-architect/", "/fractional-cto/"], "citations": [{"title": "New resources on transparency for use of AI and automated decision-making", "url": "https://www.oaic.gov.au/news/media-centre/new-resources-on-transparency-for-use-of-ai-and-automated-decision-making", "publisher": "OAIC", "date": "Sep 2026"}, {"title": "Mandatory automated decision-making disclosure requirements are coming: key takeaways from the OAIC guidance", "url": "https://www.allens.com.au/insights-news/insights/2026/10/mandatory-automated-decision-making-disclosure-requirements-are-coming-key-takeaways-from-the-oaic-guidance/", "publisher": "Allens", "date": "Oct 2026"}, {"title": "Transparency in automated decision-making: What the OAIC guidance means for your business", "url": "https://www.corrs.com.au/insights/transparency-in-automated-decision-making-what-the-oaic-guidance-means-fo